{"step_index":80,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T19:06:49Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-09-13T19:06:48Z sender=8ea3dee6-cf9c-4ba2-88dc-0b3551467a06 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=# Comprehensive Research Report: AppleCare+ for Refurbished and Second-Hand MacBook Pros in India\n\n## Executive Summary\nIn India, **you can only buy AppleCare+ for a second-hand or refurbished MacBook Pro if the machine is still within 60 days of its original retail sale date** (from Apple or an Apple Authorised Reseller). Buying from a third-party seller (e.g., Cashify, OLX, Amazon Renewed, CeX) **does not reset** the 60-day eligibility clock. \n\nFurthermore, **Apple does not operate an official Apple Certified Refurbished online store in India**. If an Apple Certified Refurbished Mac is purchased from an official Apple Store abroad (e.g., USA, UK, UAE), it is eligible for AppleCare+ within 60 days of that purchase date, and coverage is honored in India under Apple’s global Mac warranty.\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Findings\n\n### 1. Apple’s Official Policy on AppleCare+ for Certified Refurbished Macs\n* **Global / Certified Refurbished Store Policy**: \n  - All Apple Certified Refurbished devices undergo Apple's rigorous testing and refurbishment process with genuine replacement parts, receive a fresh battery and outer casing (for portables/devices where applicable), and include Apple's standard **1-Year Limited Warranty** and 90 days of complimentary technical support.\n  - Certified Refurbished Macs are fully eligible for **AppleCare+** under the exact same terms as brand-new devices. The purchaser can add AppleCare+ at checkout or within 60 days of the refurbished purchase date.\n* **Important Context for India**:\n  - Apple **does not sell Certified Refurbished Macs directly in India** (the Indian online store at `apple.com/in/shop/refurbished` does not exist and returns a 404 error).\n  - If a user imports or purchases an Apple Certified Refurbished MacBook Pro from an Apple Store in another country (such as the US, UK, Canada, Australia, etc.), they can buy AppleCare+ for it. Because Mac hardware warranties and AppleCare+ for Mac provide **global repair coverage**, repairs and accidental damage coverage are honored at Apple Stores (e.g., Apple BKC Mumbai, Apple Saket Delhi) and Apple Authorised Service Providers (AASPs) across India.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Apple’s Official Policy on AppleCare+ for Macs Bought Second-Hand from Third Parties\n* **The 60-Day Original Sale Rule**:\n  - Apple’s system calculates eligibility based strictly on the **original date of purchase (DOP)** from Apple or an Apple Authorised Reseller.\n  - Purchasing a used Mac from third-party platforms (Cashify, OLX, Quikr, CeX, Sahivalue, Amazon Renewed, or private individuals) **does NOT reset** the purchase date in Apple’s database.\n* **Scenario A: Used Mac is Within 60 Days of Original Purchase**:\n  - The new buyer **can** purchase AppleCare+ via **macOS System Settings** (`System Settings > General > AppleCare & Warranty`), online via `checkcoverage.apple.com`, or by calling Apple Support (`000800 1009009`).\n  - The Mac must pass a remote diagnostic check (or in-person inspection at an Apple Store) to ensure there is no pre-existing damage.\n* **Scenario B: Used Mac is Older than 60 Days from Original Purchase**:\n  - The Mac is **strictly ineligible** to purchase a new AppleCare+ plan. Apple India does not offer post-60-day visual inspection programs to enroll used Macs into AppleCare+.\n* **What if the Previous Owner Already Bought AppleCare+?**:\n  - **3-Year Upfront Paid Plan**: The plan is tied to the Mac's hardware serial number. Coverage transfers automatically to the new owner. To update registration records, the previous owner can transfer the agreement to the new owner by contacting Apple Support with the serial number, agreement number, and original sales receipt.\n  - **Monthly/Annual Recurring Plan**: Non-transferable. Under official Apple policy: *\"If you make monthly or annual payments for your AppleCare plan and your plan is already linked to an Apple Account, then it cannot be transferred to a new owner.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Time Limit to Purchase AppleCare+\n* **New or Apple Certified Refurbished Mac**: Within **60 days** of the purchase/delivery date.\n* **Second-Hand Mac**: Within **60 days of the FIRST retail sale date** by an authorized Apple reseller.\n* **Post-Expiry Renewal**: If an existing upfront 3-year AppleCare+ plan expires, Apple allows continuing coverage on a monthly or annual recurring basis, provided the renewal is purchased within **30 to 45 days** of the original plan's expiration date.\n\n---\n\n### 4. AppleCare+ Pricing for MacBook Pro in India\n*(Directly retrieved from Apple India's pricing API `/in/shop/mcm/product-price`)*\n\n| Device Model | Upfront Plan (3 Years) | Monthly Recurring Plan |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **MacBook Pro 14-inch** (M-Series / M4 / M5) | **₹29,900** | **₹999 / month** |\n| **MacBook Pro 16-inch** (M-Series / M4 Pro / M4 Max) | **₹40,900** | **₹1,379 / month** |\n\n*(For comparison: MacBook Air 13\" is ₹19,900 upfront / ₹699/mo; MacBook Air 15\" is ₹23,900 upfront / ₹799/mo; Mac mini is ₹10,900 upfront / ₹379/mo; Mac Studio is ₹17,900 upfront / ₹599/mo; Mac Pro is ₹52,900 upfront / ₹1,799/mo).*\n\n---\n\n### 5. What AppleCare+ Covers vs. Standard 1-Year Limited Warranty\n\n| Feature / Benefit | Standard 1-Year Limited Warranty | AppleCare+ for Mac |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Coverage Duration** | 1 Year from original purchase | **3 Years** (extendable monthly/annually) |\n| **Manufacturing Defects** | Covered (Parts & Labor at ₹0) | Covered for full 3 years (Parts & Labor at ₹0) |\n| **Accidental Damage (Drops / Spills)** | **NOT COVERED** (100% out-of-pocket, ₹50,000–₹1,20,000+) | **UNLIMITED incidents** of accidental damage protection |\n| **Screen or External Enclosure Damage Fee** | Full commercial repair cost (₹40,000–₹80,000+) | **₹8,900** flat service fee per incident |\n| **Other Accidental Damage (Liquid, Logic Board)** | Full replacement cost (₹60,000–₹1,20,000+) | **₹25,900** flat service fee per incident |\n| **Battery Service** | Only manufacturing defects | **Free (₹0)** replacement if battery retains <80% original capacity |\n| **Included Accessories** | 1 year for in-box charger & cable | 3 years for included power adapter and cable |\n| **Technical Support** | 90 days complimentary telephone support | **24/7 priority access** to Apple experts (macOS, iCloud, etc.) |\n| **Service Options in India** | Carry-in at AASPs | Carry-in, Mail-in, and Onsite service in select cities |\n| **International Coverage** | Global hardware warranty | Global repair coverage at Apple Stores/AASPs worldwide |\n\n---\n\n### 6. Key Restrictions on Buying AppleCare+ for a Used Mac\n1. **The 60-Day Hard Stop**: Third-party refurbisher invoices (from Cashify, Amazon, etc.) are **not accepted** to reset the 60-day window. If the serial number was activated >60 days ago, enrollment is permanently barred.\n2. **Diagnostic & Physical Condition Checks**: The device must pass an automated remote hardware diagnostic test (initiated via Apple Support or macOS System Settings) or an in-person physical inspection at an Apple Store / AASP. Devices with existing cracks, liquid sensor triggers, or internal component faults are denied.\n3. **No Third-Party / Unauthorized Repairs**: If the Mac was previously opened or serviced by an unauthorized repair shop or contains non-genuine Apple parts (aftermarket screen, battery, or board bypass), it is strictly disqualified from AppleCare+ and Apple service.\n4. **Activation Lock / Security Status**: The Mac must be fully unbound from the previous owner's Apple Account (no iCloud Activation Lock or MDM profile) and must not be marked as lost or stolen.\n5. **Proof of Purchase Requirements**: When attempting to purchase AppleCare+ via telephone/support channels, Apple Support may require the original authorized dealer invoice to verify the DOP. Third-party used receipts are not recognized as authorized proof of purchase.\n6. **Non-Transferable Monthly Subscriptions**: If buying a used Mac advertised as \"having AppleCare+\", ensure it is an upfront 3-year plan. If the seller has a monthly subscription, it will terminate as soon as they cancel or decouple their Apple Account.\n\n---\n\n## Official Source URLs\n- **Apple India AppleCare Overview & Pricing**: [https://www.apple.com/in/applecare/](https://www.apple.com/in/applecare/)\n- **Apple Support: Buy an AppleCare Plan**: [https://support.apple.com/en-in/101560](https://support.apple.com/en-in/101560)\n- **Apple Support: Transfer your AppleCare Plan**: [https://support.apple.com/en-in/111801](https://support.apple.com/en-in/111801)\n- **Apple Check Coverage Portal**: [https://checkcoverage.apple.com/](https://checkcoverage.apple.com/)\n- **Apple Legal: AppleCare+ Terms & Conditions (India)**: [https://www.apple.com/in/legal/sales-support/applecare/applecareplus/in/mac/](https://www.apple.com/in/legal/sales-support/applecare/applecareplus/in/mac/)\n- **Apple Certified Refurbished Program Overview**: [https://www.apple.com/shop/refurbished/about](https://www.apple.com/shop/refurbished/about)\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
